WEBVTT

00:00:05.849 --> 00:00:11.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Tuesday the twenty-second. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:21.109
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, we can hear you. I'm mainly here to complain about the broken coffee machine in the canteen. That powdered stuff is criminal.</v>

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.710
<v Callum Reid>That's not coffee, that's a test of commitment.</v>

00:00:26.649 --> 00:00:32.600
<v Marcus Hale>After the traffic on the ring road, I'd have drunk anything. Absolutely solid coming round this morning.</v>

00:00:35.079 --> 00:00:37.880
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely start, then. Tomasz, you're showing as muted.</v>

00:00:39.509 --> 00:00:44.060
<v Tomasz Nowak>There we go. Headset button and Teams button. Always pick the wrong one.</v>

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.020
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, we're all here. Quick run through what's finished first.</v>

00:00:52.429 --> 00:00:56.979
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, finished the repair on the GT2 bearing last night. That's done.</v>

00:00:59.289 --> 00:01:02.090
<v Aisha Begum>Oh, that was finished on nights, was it?</v>

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.700
<v Callum Reid>Yep, all finished. Not something we need to carry forward.</v>

00:01:08.799 --> 00:01:15.799
<v Sarah Okafor>And I signed off the inspection on the 11kV Switchboard on Tuesday — this morning, I mean. Already signed off.</v>

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:23.519
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same here, signed off the inspection on the Main Outfeed Conveyor on Tuesday. Got that closed before this call.</v>

00:01:24.239 --> 00:01:26.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, those are off the list.</v>

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:34.420
<v Tomasz Nowak>Only other thing from me, saw the pressure on the wrapper dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.500
<v Aisha Begum>It recovered without anyone touching it?</v>

00:01:39.709 --> 00:01:44.260
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, nobody touched anything. Just an observation, not bringing a repair job in.</v>

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:53.170
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Similar sort of thing, I noticed the turbine two was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down.</v>

00:01:54.959 --> 00:01:58.109
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, it had settled by handover. Nothing ongoing there.</v>

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, both noted as observations.</v>

00:02:01.489 --> 00:02:08.490
<v Sarah Okafor>The air dryer is still blocked, though. We can't get to the air dryer until production gives us a window.</v>

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:15.009
<v Callum Reid>We haven't got a window available. Still the same position, I'm afraid.</v>

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.300
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that stays parked. Not putting it into today's work.</v>

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:29.840
<v Marcus Hale>And we were going to replace the belt on the IM3, but that's been pushed to next month so ignore it.</v>

00:02:31.259 --> 00:02:34.759
<v Tomasz Nowak>Ah, right. I remembered seeing that on the old list.</v>

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:40.159
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, the old entry isn't live for today. Leave that one out.</v>

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:48.750
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Um, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the line 2 interlock by the end of the week. Normal priority.</v>

00:02:49.409 --> 00:02:54.659
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Olumide Adeyemi. That's the risk assessment update, rather than doing the interlock work itself?</v>

00:02:55.270 --> 00:03:01.219
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Exactly. I'll update the risk assessment. I'm not committing to the physical work as part of that.</v>

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:07.509
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, useful distinction. People hear 'interlock' and assume we're already into the panel.</v>

00:03:08.389 --> 00:03:11.539
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed. Normal priority, by the end of the week.</v>

00:03:12.479 --> 00:03:18.430
<v Hannah Price>I'll send the shift handover report round by end of day, while we're on the paperwork bits.</v>

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:25.770
<v Callum Reid>That's the handover report we've already got, yeah? Not another version of the thing?</v>

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:30.909
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, that one. Just sending it round, not creating a second report.</v>

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:37.469
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Hannah. Sending the shift handover report round by end of day.</v>

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:40.469
<v Hannah Price>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:46.659
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And I'll sort the training records for the new starters if I've got a spare minute.</v>

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:54.330
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Olumide Adeyemi, that's definitely an 'if you've got a spare minute' one. Not pushing the other work out.</v>

00:03:56.099 --> 00:03:59.250
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, exactly. Spare-minute job, no fixed date on that.</v>

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:04.250
<v Aisha Begum>Just the records, isn't it? Not another round of training?</v>

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:10.580
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Just sorting the training records for the new starters. That's all I'm taking on there.</v>

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:13.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, agreed on that basis.</v>

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:19.269
<v Hannah Price>I've got another one. I'll recalibrate the sensors on the line 1 TCU by Thursday.</v>

00:04:21.139 --> 00:04:24.639
<v Aisha Begum>Sorry, you clipped a bit there — line 1 TCU?</v>

00:04:26.759 --> 00:04:32.709
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, line 1 TCU. It's not an emergency but don't let it slip, that sort of priority.</v>

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:38.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed, Hannah. Recalibrate the sensors by Thursday; not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:45.019
<v Callum Reid>Right, so not a panic job. Just making sure I heard that properly.</v>

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:48.689
<v Hannah Price>No panic. I'll have that recalibration done by Thursday.</v>

00:04:49.379 --> 00:04:55.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Marc, can you run the monthly fire alarm test? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:57.389 --> 00:05:00.189
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll run the monthly fire alarm test.</v>

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:06.069
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's the routine monthly one, isn't it? Sorry, spoke over you.</v>

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.759
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, just the routine monthly test.</v>

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:15.319
<v Sarah Okafor>That's it. No emergency response implied, but don't let it slip, Marc.</v>

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.410
<v Marcus Hale>Understood. I've got that one.</v>

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:27.029
<v Sarah Okafor>And Marc, can you inspect the feedwater pump for leaks by Thursday? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:27.529 --> 00:05:31.029
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll inspect the feedwater pump for leaks by Thursday.</v>

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:33.720
<v Aisha Begum>We're talking inspection only there?</v>

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:38.750
<v Marcus Hale>Inspection for leaks, yeah. Not saying I'm replacing anything.</v>

00:05:41.149 --> 00:05:46.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. It matters but it's not urgent. Thursday is the deadline for that inspection.</v>

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:49.949
<v Marcus Hale>Fine by me. Those two are clear.</v>

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:54.519
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. That's the agreed work, then. Nothing else to squeeze in?</v>

00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:00.810
<v Aisha Begum>Only my coffee grievance, and that's not an engineering request, before anyone writes it down.</v>

00:06:01.939 --> 00:06:05.439
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good. I don't think there's a calibration setting for 'drinkable'.</v>

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:13.819
<v Callum Reid>And just checking the finished bits don't get copied back into the open list. The GT2 bearing's definitely done.</v>

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:20.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. Finished items stay closed, observations are just observations, and the blocked and postponed bits stay out.</v>

00:06:23.199 --> 00:06:24.600
<v Hannah Price>All clear here, thanks.</v>

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:28.379
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Thanks, everyone. I'll let you get off Teams.</v>
